# Committed counterpart of the clean-IP pattern file.
#
# The scan matches against a pattern list the author holds privately. Only its SHA-256 digest is
# published — recorded in every attestation — so two runs are comparable without the list itself
# ever being disclosed. Publishing the patterns would defeat their purpose.
#
# What a third party CAN verify, without the list:
#   - the check's scan scope: tracked file contents, paths in history, historical blob contents
#     (bytes, not text), commit metadata, and annotated tag messages
#   - its fail-closed behaviour: an absent or truncated pattern list is a FAILURE, never a pass
#   - that it is load-bearing: the harness self-test plants a matching term in the tree, in a
#     historical blob, and in a path, and REQUIRES the check to fail each time
#
# Run `python3 harness/validate.py --self-test` to see those mutations pass or fail.
#
# A minimum pattern count is enforced so a truncated list cannot silently succeed.
